  "note": "Consumer betting brands in the US, matched to state regulator listings by DOMAIN first and brand name second. Domain first because the listings are not written the same way twice: Connecticut lists plain names ('DraftKings'), Michigan and Pennsylvania list 'Brand (domain)', and New Jersey lists bare domains with no brand name at all ('nj.betmgm.com/en/casino'). Name matching alone silently returns zero for every New Jersey casino. The brand list itself is built by hand, not by fuzzy matching: regulators name whatever the licence was issued to, which is sometimes the consumer brand, sometimes the corporate entity behind it (Roar Digital for BetMGM, Hillside for bet365, Rush Street Interactive for BetRivers), and sometimes the venue holding the skin. Merging on a shared word would fold Bally Bet into Bally's Dover, a BetRivers skin. Anything unmatched is left off the brand pages and stays on its state page, where it is already sourced. B2B suppliers (Kambi, NYX, GAN, Strive) are deliberately absent: they are not books a reader can sign up to. Counts are 'named by N state regulators', not 'operating in N states' — the lists are what each regulator publishes and some lag a rebrand.",
